rem Skew-cost Coding
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=219
rem Find the least total cost of a
rem prefix-free code of N words, where
rem a 0 costs 1 and a 1 costs 4

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option N integer = 1000000000

rem Keep the number of leaves of each
rem cost. Splitting a leaf of cost c
rem into leaves c + 1 and c + 4 adds
rem c + 5 to the total and one leaf, so
rem cheapest leaves are split first,
rem a whole cost level at a time.
Cnt = array shape 2000 fill 0
Cnt 1 = 1
Cnt 4 = 1
Leaves = 2
Total = 5
for C in 1 to 1990
  K = Cnt C min (N - Leaves)
  if K greater 0
    Cnt C -= K
    Cnt (C + 1) += K
    Cnt (C + 4) += K
    Leaves += K
    Total += K * (C + 5)
  end
end
Answer = Total
Answer print
